          %h2#finitely_generated_flat_modules Finitely generated flat modules
          %p Thanks to the general structure theorem of flat modules, one gets
          %p
          #FinitelyPresentedFlatIsProjective.num_cor
            %h6 Corollary
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+presented"} finitely presented
              module
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is flat
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is projective
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    M\;\text{is flat}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    M\;\text{is projective}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is at the same time finitely presented and a filtered colimit of finitely generated free modules, the identity morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \to M
              must factor as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \to F \to M
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a finitely generated free module. This implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is projective.
          %p In many cases, “finite presentation” can be replaced with “finite generation”.
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              (When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is local)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated module
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local ring
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is flat
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is free
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    M\;\text{is flat}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    M\;\text{is free}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Matsumara"} Matsumara, Theorem 7.10
          %p Thus we see that finitely generated flat modules are locally free in the weak sense. Let us recall the definition of locally free modules and their relation with projective modules.
          #LocallyFreeModule.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              An
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is called a
              %strong locally free module in the weak sense
              if for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+ideal"} prime ideal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔭
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p} \hookrightarrow R
              the localised module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi 𝔭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_\mathfrak{p}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+ring"} localization
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi 𝔭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_\mathfrak{p}
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated module
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                is projective ;
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                is locally free in the weak sense and the rank function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔭
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔭
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p} \mapsto \mathrm{r}(\mathfrak{p})
                is locally constant.
            %p
          %p Then one has the following characterisation of finitely generated flat modules.
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated module
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is flat
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is locally free in the weak sense
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    M\;\text{is flat}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    M\;\text{is locally free in the weak sense}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p This characterisation can be strengthened in two very large cases
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              (When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is Noetherian) If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+ring"} Noetherian ring
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated module
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is flat
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is projective
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    M\;\text{is flat}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    M\;\text{is projective}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Over a Noetherian ring all finitely generated modules are finitely presented. So this is a simple consequence of Corollary (
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FinitelyPresentedFlatIsProjective"}>
              )
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              (When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is an integral domain) If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated module
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is flat
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is projective
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    M\;\text{is flat}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    M\;\text{is projective}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Given two prime ideals
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔭
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi 𝔮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p} \subset \mathfrak{q}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔭
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔮
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{r}(\mathfrak{p}) = \mathrm{r}(\mathfrak{q})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is an integral domain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0)
              is a prime ideal and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi 𝔭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0) \subset \mathfrak{p}
              for every prime ideal
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔭
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔭
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p} \mapsto \mathrm{r}(\mathfrak{p})
              is thus constant.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The proof of the above proposition shows that the same result is true for every ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              with a unique minimal ideal.
          %p In the general case, it is not true that all finitely generated flat modules are projective.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counter-example"}> counter-example
              ) Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \prod_{i = 0}^\infty k
              be an infinite product of fields. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi k
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \oplus_{i = 0}^\infty k \subset R
              its ideal.
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/I
              is a finitely generated
              = succeed "-module," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            The class of commutative rings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            over which all finitely generated flat modules are projective has been determined in the 1970s.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a commutative ring. The following two are equivalent :
            %ol
              %li
                Every finitely generated flat
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %li
                Every sequence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_0, a_1, \dots)
                of elements of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{n+1} a_n = a_n
                for every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq n
            %p
          %p
            One can see Gena Puninski; Philipp Rothmaler (2004).
            = succeed "." do
              %em When every finitely generated flat module is projective
          %h2#countably_presented_flat_modules Countably presented flat modules
          %p As we have seen finitely presented flat module are always projective ; their projective dimension is equal to zero. For countably presented flat modules, the dimension cannot exceed one.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              A countably presented flat module has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+dimension"} projective dimension
              inferior or equal to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be a countably generated flat module. Being flat, it can be written as an inductive limit of finitely generated free modules
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_A M_\alpha
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is also countably presented, there exists a countable cofinal filtered subset
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \subset A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathbb{N}
            %p
              Denoting by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_n : M_n \to M_{n+1}
              the transition maps, one can build the short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to \oplus M_n \overset{G}{\to} \oplus M_n \to M \to 0
            %p
              where the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              restricted to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n
              is given by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 - g_n
          %h2#classes_of_rings_related_to_flatness Classes of rings, related to flatness
          %p
            As we have seen, there is not much difference between flat modules and projective modules in the finitely generated case. The notion of flatness starts becoming really distinct in the case of infinitely generated modules. For example the
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            is flat (since it is torsion-free) but far from being free.
          %p
            On the other side, for infinitely generated module, the notion of projectivity is less useful since for example the module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[[X]]
            which is the infinite product of copies of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            is
            %em not free
            but still flat. It is common to encounter infinitely generated flat modules and uncommon to encounter infinitely generated projective modules.
          %p To better understand the general notion of flatness from a geometric perspective, very early after the definition of the notion, two questions have been asked
          %ol
            %li A product of torsion-free modules is always torsion-free, is it true for flat modules ?
            %li
              What type of rings
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              have all their modules flat?
            %li
              For what type of rings
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is it true that all torsion-free modules are flat?
            %li For what type of rings can flat modules be the filtered union of their finitely generated projective submodules?
          %h3#coherent_rings Coherent rings
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For a commutative ring
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a
                = succeed "\u202F;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+ring"} coherent ring
              %li
                the product of a family of flat
                = succeed "-modules" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \Rightarrow 2
              \. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Q_\alpha\}_{\alpha \in A}
              be a set of flat
              = succeed "-modules." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \otimes \prod_\alpha Q_\alpha \to \prod_\alpha Q_\alpha
              is injective for every finitely generated ideal
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is coherent every such ideal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+presented+module"} finitely presented module
              and thus the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \otimes \prod_\alpha Q_\alpha \to \prod_\alpha Q_\alpha
              is the product of the maps
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi α
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \otimes Q_\alpha \to Q_\alpha
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_\alpha
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \Rightarrow 1
              \. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset R
              be a finitely generated ideal. Using one of the equivalent characterisations of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+presented+modules"} finitely presented modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \otimes R^A \to I^A
              is an isomorphism, for every set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^A
              is a flat module, the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \otimes R^A \to R^A
              is injective and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is finitely generated, its image is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi I
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^A
          %h3#absolutely_flat_rings Absolutely flat rings
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              We say that a ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is absolutely flat if every
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              The following propositions are equivalent for a commutative ring
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is absolutely flat;
              %li
                every ideal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset R
                is idempotent, i.e.
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi I
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^2 = I
              %li
                for every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in R
                there exists an element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in R
                such that
                = succeed "\u202F;" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = x^2 y
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi 𝔭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_\mathfrak{p}
                is a field for every prime ideal
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔭
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p} \subset R
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi 𝔪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_\mathfrak{m}
                is a field for every maximal ideal
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔪
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{m} \subset R
            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              2. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset R
              be any ideal of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is absolutely flat, the
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/I
              must be flat. One has
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Tor
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi I
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Tor_1(R/I, R/I) \simeq I/{I^2}
            %p
              the ideal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              must thus be idempotent;
            %p
              2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              3. For every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              must be idempotent, that is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)(x) = (x)
              which means that there must exist
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              such that
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = x^2y
            %p
              3
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              4. Let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝔭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathfrak{p}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in R
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mi u
                      %mi r
                      %mo =
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r u r = r
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi u
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r ( 1 - u r ) = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝔭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u r \in \mathfrak{p}
              it follows that the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi u
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1- u r
              is invertible in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi 𝔭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_\mathfrak{p}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              is null in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi 𝔭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_\mathfrak{p}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi 𝔭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_\mathfrak{p}
              is trivial.
            %p
              4
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              5. Obvious.
            %p
              5
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              1. Because flatness is a local property.
            %p
          %h3#semihereditary_rings Semi-hereditary rings
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Recall that a commutative ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is
              %span.newWikiWord
                semi-hereditary
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/semi-hereditary"} ?
              if every finitely generated ideal is projective.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              For a commutative ring
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is
                = succeed "\u202F;" do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    semi-hereditary
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/semi-hereditary"} ?
              %li
                The total ring of fractions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Q}(R)
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is absolutely flat and for every maximal ideal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{m}
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi 𝔪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_\mathfrak{m}
                is a
                = succeed "\u202F;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation+ring"} valuation ring
              %li
                Every torsion-free
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              First, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a local ring, this follows from the equivalent characterisations of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation+rings"} valuation rings
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \Rightarrow 2
              \. Every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi 𝔪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_\mathfrak{m}
              is a localisation of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Q}(R)
              is absolutely flat, it shall be enough to show that for every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi r
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 = r x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              is projective. As a consequence the annihilator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ann
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ann(x) \subset R
              is a direct summand, so there exists an idempotent
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \in R
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ann
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ann(x) = (\pi)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \coloneqq x + \pi
              is a regular element such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi r
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 = r x
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \Rightarrow 3
              \. When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Q}(R)
              is absolutely flat, being torsion-free becomes a local property, as it is for flatness.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3 \Rightarrow 1
              \. Torsion-free modules are stable under product, so it follows that flat modules are also stable under product which means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is coherent. Then every finitely generated ideal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset R
              is finitely presented. Since they are also torsion-free, they are flat and thus projective.
          %h2#Examles Examples
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PID"} PID
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              is flat (regarded as a
              = succeed "-module)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion-free
            %p
              In particular, the modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[[X]]
              are flat.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The ring of power series
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[[X]]
              (which as an
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %ol
              %li It is always torsion-free;
              %li
                it is a flat
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+ring"} coherent ring
              %li
                it is almost never free. In particular
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[[X]]
                is not free.
            %p
          %p
            For the flatness of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[[X]]
            see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Chase"}
                %em> Direct products of modules
                , Theorem 2.1
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be an integral domain, with field of fractions
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a flat
              = succeed "-module," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi r
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mi r
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K = \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_r \;\frac{1}{r}\;R
            %p
              of free
              = succeed "-modules." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              is an idempotent element of a commutative ring
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/(\pi)
              is projective, hence flat.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+morphism+of+schemes"} flat morphism of schemes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+resolution+lemma"} flat resolution lemma
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"}> projective object
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+presentation"} projective presentation
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+cover"} projective cover
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+resolution"} projective resolution
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"}> injective object
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+presentation"} injective presentation
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+envelope"} injective envelope
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+resolution"} injective resolution
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+module"} injective module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"}> free object
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+resolution"} free resolution
            %li
              %p
                flat object,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+resolution"} flat resolution
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⇒
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective module
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⇒
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
                %strong flat module
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⇒
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion-free+module"} torsion-free module
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Flat modules (“modules plats” in French) where first defined in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GAGA"} GAGA
          %ul#GAGA
            %li
              Jean-Pierre Serre,
              %em Géométrie Algébrique et Géométrie Analytique
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/article/AIF_1956__6__1_0.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Original articles include
          %ul#RaynaudGruson
            %li
              %p
                Shizuo Endo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On flat modules over commutative rings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jmsj/1261060583"} EUCLID
            %li
              %p
                Shizuo Endo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On semi-hereditary rings
            %li
              %p
                Michel Raynaud, Laurent Gruson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Critères de platitude et de projectivité
          %ul
            %li
              S. Jondrup,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Flat and projective modules
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mscand.dk/article.php?id=2456"} pdf
          %p
            The characterization of flat modules as filtered colimits of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+modules"} projective modules
            is due to
          %ul#Lazard
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Lazard"}> Daniel Lazard
              ,
              %em Sur les modules plats
              C. R. Acad. Sci. Paris 258, 6313–6316 (1964)
          %p For a general account see for instance section 3.2 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Weibel"}> Charles Weibel
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/An+Introduction+to+Homological+Algebra"} An Introduction to Homological Algebra
          %p For more details see
          %ul#Matsumara
            %li Matsumura’s CRT book
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li
              Arthur Ogus,
              %em Flatness – a brief overview
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~ogus/Math%20_256B--09/Supplements/flat.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Further resources include
          %ul#Chase
            %li
              %p
                MO discussion
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/33522/flatness-and-local-freeness"} flatness and local freeness
            %li
              %p
                Stephen Chase,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/tran/1960-097-03/S0002-9947-1960-0120260-3/S0002-9947-1960-0120260-3.pdf"} Direct product of modules
        .revisedby
          %p
